 one particular case, either through a patient-level predicate frame (a presentational, diagnostic, or \"with\"-complement construction attributing the condition to a person) or through a restrictor modifier naming a specific genetic locus, causative agent, or anatomical site, **THEN** label it **SpecificDisease**. Do not assign DiseaseClass based on the head noun's morphology or hypernym status alone.\n  - **Negative Constraint:** Do **NOT** apply this rule when the category-type mention is used at the kind or generic level, such as a feature inventory shared across a syndrome or population, a taxonomic or definitional statement about a class, or a trait list not tied to an individual's diagnosis. In those cases, DiseaseClass remains correct. Also do not apply it when the category term functions as a pre-nominal modifier of another noun rather than as the head denoting a condition, since the Modifier definition governs that case. Proper-name anchors (eponyms and acronyms) are already SpecificDisease and need no category check.\n  - **Scope:** This rule governs only the label choice. It does not change span boundaries or merge items into a CompositeMention.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2318, "output_tokens": 2220, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1759}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}